From: PinePhone firmware
Subject: [PATCH] bar: no mask for an indicator shorter than the radius

An indicator shorter than the bar's rounded ends (a slider at a low value:
volume 2 of 16, brightness at its minimum, a progress bar starting) was drawn
on a layer clipped to the background's radius with a rectangle mask, which
the OpenGL ES draw unit does not support: it drew the layer unclipped and
logged an error on every redraw. Such an indicator is now drawn directly with
its own radius, as it appeared. Gradients and images still use masks.
---
--- a/src/widgets/bar/lv_bar.c
+++ b/src/widgets/bar/lv_bar.c
@@ -610,7 +610,10 @@
     else if(indic_radius >= bg_radius) radius_issue = false;
     else if(lv_area_is_in(&indic_area, &bar_coords, bg_radius)) radius_issue = false;
 
-    if(radius_issue || mask_needed) {
+    /*Only a gradient or an image is clipped with masks: an indicator shorter than the
+     *background's radius is drawn as it is, with its own smaller radius. The OpenGL ES
+     *draw unit cannot draw masks.*/
+    if(mask_needed) {
         if(!radius_issue) {
             /*Draw only the shadow*/
             lv_draw_rect_dsc_t draw_rect_tmp_dsc = draw_rect_dsc;
